messages:
alex: Heads up — sampleapp rerank is failing in Node when using the batching helper. Error: vectors getting padded/truncated and the API returns 400 (expected dim 1536, got 1530). Anyone run into parity issues between SDKs?

maya: Yep, saw this earlier. Node helper was doing an integer join+pad step that accidentally dropped trailing floats on retry. :facepalm:

sam: Can you paste the minimal repro? Curious if its a padding bug or an index shuffle during retries.

alex: Repro (in our sampleapp):
```js
// simplified pseudocode
const batch = batchHelper.prepare(vectors) // sometimes returns length mismatch
await client.embeddings.create({model: 'text-embedding-3-small', input: batch})
// error: { code: 400, message: 'vector dimension mismatch: expected 1536, got 1530' }
```

jordana: That looks like the helper is trimming NaN/undefined entries when converting typed arrays. On retries we end up merging two batches and the ordering/padding logic runs twice.

leo-bot: Automated test run: sampleapp/ci embedding-integration failed on node-16 (flaky) — see https://ci.redwood.ai/9876 (related?)

maya: Two quick mitigations: 1) add a pre-send validator in SDK: ensure vectors.every(v => v.length === expectedDim) and throw early; 2) normalize helper to explicitly pad with 0.0 and use Float32Array consistently.

sam: Also watch auth/retry behavior — we have an issue where a retry will re-append a batch instead of replacing, causing duplicate entries and dimension shifts when batches are recomposed. Filed as #4567.

alex: OK i'm going to open a small PR that: adds a validator, fixes the pad logic, and updates the sampleapp onboarding doc to mention expected dims. Will add a unit test that fuzzes vector lengths.

jordana: Nice. For the PR, include a tiny helper:
```js
function normalizeVectors(vecs, expectedDim) {
  return vecs.map(v => {
    if (v.length > expectedDim) return v.slice(0, expectedDim);
    if (v.length < expectedDim) {
      const out = new Float32Array(expectedDim);
      out.set(v);
      return out;
    }
    return v;
  });
}
```

maya: We should also add an example in the SDK README showing the shape check and a one-liner for python/node parity. Small note in changelog. :thumbsup:

sam: Ill sync with @eng-sdk to make sure the retry logic replaces batches instead of appending. If people want to avoid the immediate fix, a quick workaround in the sampleapp is to run the normalizeVectors before calling the client.

alex: Thanks everyone — i'll tag you in the PR (#7890) and add the sampleapp patch. Planning to release the patch to the sampleapp tomorrow and cut a patch release on the node SDK if tests pass.

maya: :rocket: ping me for a review.

jordana: Adding note for support: earlier customer hit this as well (CS-312) during onboarding. Will update the KB with the workaround.

sam: Great. I'll follow up on #4567 and link to the PR.

alex: Closing loop — PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sampleapp/pull/7890. Will post release notes once cut.

maya: Nice work!
